What it does (全線一條真實鏈路，但不碰任何真實資料):
  1. logins via /api/auth/login with --creds-env (STUDENT_ID/SPASSWORD file,
     chmod 600, outside the repo; password never printed, never stored);
  2. seeds ONE synthetic LOCAL catalog row 課號 ZZ999999 (a course code the
     school does NOT have) so our own preview's 無課號 gate does not fire —
     the row is marked QA 探針 and DELETED in a finally-block (reversible,
     local-only; psql seed/drop contract verified tonight);
  3. previews ADD of ZZ999999 — expected to PASS with quota warning
     (quota_snapshot; remaining=3 > 0 so no remaining_zero noise);
  4. confirms with the freshly re-typed password (SSO2 re-auth RIGHT NOW,
     fresh jar overwrites the session's selcrs entry);
  5. polls GET /api/write/jobs/{job_id} until terminal (≤6 min);
  6. EXPECTS a SCHOOL-SIDE BUSINESS FAILURE on the audit row
     (outcome=failed with the school's own message) — the school is asked
     to add a course it does not have, so it must say no: the wire, the
     form-replay worker, the response parser, and the audit ledger are all
     proven live, with ZERO modification to the user's real selections;
  7. prints the write_audit row (course/action/outcome/school_msg excerpt/
     stuid_hash truncated to 12 chars + created_at).

